/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/llms-full.txt
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Per-page Markdown mirrors (<path>/index.md), emitted by the
# [outputFormats.Markdown] block in hugo.toml.
#
# ONE splat, not two. Cloudflare: "When matching, a splat pattern — signified
# by an asterisk (*) — will greedily match all characters. You may only
# include a single splat in the URL." The splat is greedy across "/", so this
# single rule covers /changelog/index.md and /reference/http-api/index.md
# alike. An earlier version of this file used /**/*.md; two splats are not
# permitted and such a rule does not apply — silently, with no build error and
# no deploy warning. If a .md response ever comes back without the headers
# below, count the asterisks first.
#
# Content-Type must be stated explicitly: the /* rule above sets
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, so nothing may be inferred from the body.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is the actual, and only, protection against these mirrors being
# indexed alongside the HTML pages they duplicate. Do not weaken it on the
# theory that Google does not index text/markdown — Google determines file
# type from Content-Type but reserves the right to fall back to the extension
# or re-parse when that header is "missing or incorrect", so the exemption
# evaporates the moment the line above does. nofollow is not decoration
# either: it stops a crawler chasing the rewritten in-body links.
#
# Do NOT translate this into a robots.txt Disallow. A Disallow would block the
# AI agents these files exist for, and Google never reads indexing rules on a
# URL it is not allowed to crawl — the noindex would go unseen.
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
